    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** leading the charge, posting an elite 81.88 efficiency score. His favorable matchup against Reynaldo L\u00f3pez\u2014coupled with a 16% park factor boost and a prime three-hole placement\u2014makes him our anchor. **Jackson Merrill** (71.56) and **Drake Baldwin** (71.83) round out our top-tier plays. **Drake Baldwin** benefits significantly from the leadoff spot and a generous 4.37 xERA matchup, while **Jackson Merrill** provides stability in the middle of the order, leveraging a 14% SP skill advantage against Junk to sustain high-floor production in the absence of elite stolen base opportunities.\n\nRegarding our tactical adjustments, we are leaning into specific environmental and order-based edges. **Denzer Guzman** (53.32) remains a start primarily due to a 19% SP skill advantage and a wind-out benefit that mitigates his lower batting order placement. Meanwhile, the decision to bench **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (47.58) was the most difficult; despite a decent profile, the negative dynamic platoon adjustment against Drake and a sub-optimal eighth-place assignment pushed him just below the threshold required to displace the higher-ceiling utility of **Andy Pages** (60.70). **Andy Pages** maintains his spot due to the high-leverage leadoff/two-hole proximity and favorable overall projection, even with a minor efficiency tax due to elite catcher framing.\n\nWe remain cautious of several variables that could compress our ceiling. **Sam Antonacci** (48.70) presents the highest risk of the active starters; his efficiency is hampered by a significant -16% SP skill penalty against Blanco. Additionally, while we are tracking the daily lineup potential, keep an eye on **Heliot Ramos** (55.10); while he benefits from a wind-out scenario, his value is throttled by a -2% SB risk associated with the opposing catcher\u2019s holding capability. We will monitor these slots closely as the games progress to preserve our remaining game caps, ensuring that we only deploy marginal assets when the projected efficiency comfortably clears the 40.0 floor.",
